# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:7
translate italian counselorconversation5_0c2aa4f4:

    # pc "I kind of miss Brazil."
    pc "Mi manca un po’ il Brasile."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:8
translate italian counselorconversation5_2ec566c7:

    # sc "I bet. Was it nice there?"
    sc "Ci scommetto. Era bello lì?"

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:9
translate italian counselorconversation5_ef088408:

    # pc "It was, most of the time."
    pc "Lo era, il più delle volte."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:10
translate italian counselorconversation5_ffefa487:

    # sc "Most of the time?"
    sc "Il più delle volte?"

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:11
translate italian counselorconversation5_f6155a33:

    # pc "Well the places that I stayed at were very nice."
    pc "Beh, i posti in cui ho soggiornato erano molto belli."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:12
translate italian counselorconversation5_444ece6f:

    # pc "But Brazil has a sort of split-personality."
    pc "Ma il Brasile ha una sorta di doppia personalità."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:13
translate italian counselorconversation5_9247b82f:

    # pc "It's absolutely beautiful in most of the places that I stayed."
    pc "È assolutamente bellissimo nella maggior parte dei posti in cui ho soggiornato."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:14
translate italian counselorconversation5_6ce76dfd:

    # pc "But occasionally, I saw the other side, where people were so poor and hungry and had no way to better themselves."
    pc "Ma ogni tanto ho visto l’altro lato, dove le persone erano così povere e affamate e non avevano modo di migliorare la propria situazione."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:15
translate italian counselorconversation5_64352ea1:

    # sc "That must have been eye-opening."
    sc "Deve essere stata un’esperienza che ti ha aperto gli occhi."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:16
translate italian counselorconversation5_ad0a9fab:

    # pc "It was. I know that people are like that in places,"
    pc "Lo è stata. So che in certi posti le persone vivono così,"

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:17
translate italian counselorconversation5_b47c5612:

    # pc "But it was so strange to see all of that, then go back to the dorm where I was living and nobody seemed to care."
    pc "Ma era così strano vedere tutto quel disagio e poi tornare al dormitorio dove vivevo e vedere che a nessuno sembrava importare."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:18
translate italian counselorconversation5_ba9df9c6:

    # sc "We tend to ignore the nasty things in life that don't affect us personally."
    sc "Tendiamo a ignorare gli aspetti sgradevoli della vita che non ci riguardano personalmente."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:19
translate italian counselorconversation5_34e34dc1:

    # sc "It's a sort of coping mechanism. If we were constantly worried about every bad thing happening, we'd probably have a stroke."
    sc "È una sorta di meccanismo di difesa. Se fossimo costantemente preoccupati per ogni cosa negativa che accade, probabilmente avremmo un infarto."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:20
translate italian counselorconversation5_e46768d7:

    # pc "I guess so, it's just hard to put some of that stuff out of my mind."
    pc "Immagino di sì, è solo che faccio fatica a togliermi certe cose dalla testa."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:21
translate italian counselorconversation5_2426cfe6:

    # sc "You shouldn't. You should keep it there. It will make you a better person."
    sc "Non dovresti. Dovresti tenerle a mente. Ti renderanno una persona migliore."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:22
translate italian counselorconversation5_4a449be8:

    # sc "Know that these things are happening, and know that you are privileged to have the life that you have."
    sc "Sii consapevole che queste cose stanno accadendo e renditi conto di quanto sei fortunato ad avere la vita che hai."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:23
translate italian counselorconversation5_e88d7ffc:

    # pc "You're right."
    pc "Hai ragione."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:25
translate italian counselorconversation5_067380d2:

    # sc "You have a good heart. Have you seen The Breakfast Club?"
    sc "Hai un cuore d’oro. Hai visto “The Breakfast Club”?"

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:28
translate italian counselorconversation5_a6773fcb:

    # pc "Sure. Everybody has seen that, right?"
    pc "Certo. L’hanno visto tutti, vero?"

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:30
translate italian counselorconversation5_8c93b784:

    # pc "I haven't seen it."
    pc "Io non l’ho visto."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:31
translate italian counselorconversation5_14e2d7b8:

    # sc "Well there's a line in it that Ally Sheedy says."
    sc "Beh, c’è una battuta che dice Ally Sheedy."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:32
translate italian counselorconversation5_314554fe:

    # sc "She says, \"When you grow up, your heart dies.\""
    sc "Dice: «Quando cresci, il tuo cuore muore»."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:33
translate italian counselorconversation5_67060d07:

    # sc "And it's true for a lot of people. As they grow up, they become jaded and cynical and stop caring about things."
    sc "Ed è vero per molte persone. Man mano che crescono, diventano disillusi e cinici e smettono di interessarsi alle cose."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:34
translate italian counselorconversation5_9123a037:

    # sc "But you're still young. You have a good heart. Don't let it die, okay?"
    sc "Ma tu sei ancora giovane. Hai un cuore buono. Non lasciarlo morire, ok?"

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:35
translate italian counselorconversation5_dd9a629d:

    # pc "I won't."
    pc "Non lo farò."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:37
translate italian counselorconversation5_37653c95:

    # sc "Okay, well you better get to class."
    sc "Ok, beh, è meglio che tu vada a lezione."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:38
translate italian counselorconversation5_a8c43555:

    # pc "Okay, I'll see you next time Gertrude."
    pc "Ok, ci vediamo la prossima volta, Gertrude."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:39
translate italian counselorconversation5_1b784c07:

    # sc "Bye, [pcname]."
    sc "Ciao, [pcname]."

# game/Scenes/CounselorChats/Conversations/5 - Brazil.rpy:40
translate italian counselorconversation5_e4b88e88:

    # "With that, I stand up and head to class."
    "Detto questo, mi alzo e mi dirigo verso l’aula."

